Sushil,

Murali is travelling; I'll respond on his behalf.

RFI-018 response:

(i) **Lintel:** For penetrations > 500 × 250 mm (i.e., Penetration 1), provide a lintel:
   - Lintel size: 600 × 300 × 1200 mm (M30 RCC + 4 × 12mm bars top + 4 × 12mm bars bottom + 8mm stirrups @ 150 c/c)
   - Detail: see Drawing S-006 Detail D5 for typical lintel detail

   For Penetrations 2 + 3 (600 × 200), a sleeve is acceptable IF placed at least 300mm below the slab. The slab itself acts as a load distributor. NO lintel required.

(ii) **Fire-stop classification:** Both server halls are designated as 2-hour fire compartments. Per NBC 2016 Section 13.3 + IS 12777:1989, the fire-stopping must be rated **at least 2 hours (FS-120)**.

(iii) **Recommended product:**
   - 3M Fire Barrier Sealant CP-25 (or equivalent BIS-certified product)
   - Application: full annulus around each cable + tray; mineral wool packing followed by intumescent sealant
   - Inspection requirement: visual inspection per penetration at install + smoke test (qualitative) prior to handover

Please ensure the contractor (Mahalaxmi/Phoenix) provides certified installer + retains test certificate for each penetration. Acme's commissioning team will verify.

Anand — for site coordination, please cast lintel for Penetration 1 in the next slab pour cycle (week of 22 Aug) and provide sleeve formwork for Penetrations 2 + 3.

